Package: selectFiberseqLociWorkflow
Type: Package
Title: Select and Analyze Single-Molecule Fiber-seq Loci
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("Crystal", "Shan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "crystalshan2002@gmail.com")
Description: Select genomic loci from coordinates or transcript annotations and
    analyze processed Fiber-seq modification and footprint tracks in R.
    Represent genomic positions with GRanges and sparse modification assays
    with RangedSummarizedExperiment, keeping read metadata and footprint ranges
    aligned in colData. Provide optional Manhattan-distance Leiden clustering,
    accessibility profiles, locus visualizations, and a small reproducible
    example without requiring an external workflow engine.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.4.0)
Imports: BiocGenerics, GenomeInfoDb, GenomicRanges, IRanges, S4Vectors,
    SummarizedExperiment, rtracklayer, Rsamtools, Matrix, data.table, dplyr,
    igraph, withr, ggplot2, ComplexHeatmap, methods, stats, utils, grDevices
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown, BiocCheck
VignetteBuilder: knitr
biocViews: Epigenetics, Sequencing, Clustering,
    DataImport, Visualization, Software
URL: https://github.com/CrystalShann/plot_selected_Fiber-seq_loci
BugReports: https://github.com/CrystalShann/plot_selected_Fiber-seq_loci/issues
